# Deploy config (Compose / Artalk YAML / nginx)

## docker-compose

- Pin image tags; avoid `:latest` in production.
- Do not bake secrets into the compose file; use `${VAR}` from `.env`.
- Persist data with a named or bind volume under `./data` (gitignored).
- Keep the service on a loopback-published port unless there is a clear reason not to.

## artalk.yml

- Prefer documenting non-secret knobs here; keep `app_key` and admin credentials out of git when possible (env override).
- Match `locale`, `timezone`, `site_default`, `site_url`, and trusted domains to the live blog/comments hosts.
- Do not flip `debug: true` in committed production config.

## nginx

- Preserve `Host`, `X-Real-IP`, `X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Forwarded-Proto` for Artalk/proxy IP trust.
- `proxy_pass` must target the loopback port from compose.
- Keep `server_name` equal to the public comments hostname.
- TLS termination may live outside this file; do not invent a full certbot stack unless asked.
